# Git on Windows checks out CRLF by default, which breaks two things here.
#
# `zig fmt --check` wants LF and reported every source file as misformatted, so
# the Windows CI job failed thirty seconds in on formatting alone. And a shell
# script with CRLF line endings does not run: the interpreter sees the trailing
# carriage return as part of the shebang path. install.sh, the plugin launcher
# and the hook are all shell, and all of them ship to users.
#
# Normalise to LF in the repository and on checkout, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything that must never be line-ending translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
